          "note": "Read complete KM physical pages 23–24 and individually displayed the matching image. The source defines matroid fibres through quotients of intersections of upper Klyachko flats and explicitly says the quotient map itself is unclear. Lemma 6.2 gives an induction on the intersection lattice identifying fibre bases with adapted matroid bases; Lemma 6.3 identifies global-section characters with supporting vertices. Definition 6.4 and Theorem 6.5 give exactly the finite witness criterion used by Chern flow: a basis on each cone with its characters in the associated parliament polyhedra. Theorem 6.6's printed statement omits the N-th power, while its proof and quantified wording require sufficiently large ample twists; do not copy that typo. Definition 6.8 is an alternating sum of ranks, not constructed higher tropical sheaf cohomology. No claim that these structures have ordinary vector-bundle exact sequences."
        },
