          "note": "Read complete MTY physical page 23 and individually displayed the matching image. Read the upper-bound-in-dominance-poset proof with its Fomin–Greene input and the precise Rothe-diagram Schubitope conjecture 5.13. This conjecture is stronger than ordinary SNP and is not marked solved merely from Chern flow's support theorem. The full 11-page MTY selection is complete; actual v2 numbering differs from possible published numbering, so any book reference will identify the exact version or describe the proposition unambiguously."
        },
        {
          "UTC": "2026-10-07T21:33:48.153543+00:00",
          "sheet": 43,
          "source_id": "Meszaros_Setiabrata_St_Dizier",
          "physical_pages": [
            1,
            2
          ],
          "source_PDF_SHA256": "1b42aa516836b2cabe76dd2804b9926e16bc5f8cf18565c28959f8ce571ee5c1",
          "image_SHA256": "2bc2d6fbf6ed770880fc1dde313b558a70918ce9a89f97c905420b849cba2d5c",
          "complete_text_SHA256": "7c204353199a95e3f6bccf98919b55ca2b37f054e7105f1d13c91fc34fd273dc",
          "complete_selected_text_actually_read": true,
          "matching_sheet_image_individually_displayed": true,
          "reading_mode": "fresh_complete_selected_text_and_matching_image",
          "note": "Read complete MSD physical pages 1–2 and individually displayed the matching image. Verified v1 dated 24 January 2022 and all three authors. Exact Conjectures 1.1–1.4 concern support augmentation, one-step augmentation, coordinatewise interval closure, and SNP plus generalized-polymatroid Newton polytopes. Chern flow's M-natural-convex ordinary Grothendieck support addresses this group of support statements. Conjectures 1.5–1.6 instead concern signed coefficients/Möbius functions and partial coefficient sums; these do not follow merely from support convexity and are not marked settled by this import. The historical suggestion of double-polynomial lifts is likewise outside the checked conclusion."
        },
        {
          "UTC": "2026-10-07T21:33:58.122014+00:00",
          "sheet": 44,
          "source_id": "Meszaros_Setiabrata_St_Dizier",
          "physical_pages": [
            3
          ],
          "source_PDF_SHA256": "1b42aa516836b2cabe76dd2804b9926e16bc5f8cf18565c28959f8ce571ee5c1",
          "image_SHA256": "4f02f934168ea8858877b3d1d9cd48cb38ba512b78b2bfcd7ecd051a89101d3f",
          "complete_text_SHA256": "35e4cf4a639693da3147a9c4bd263da0bbb1e76fc2e8ce1ee6658b82673e009a",
          "complete_selected_text_actually_read": true,
          "matching_sheet_image_individually_displayed": true,
          "reading_mode": "fresh_complete_selected_text_and_matching_image",
          "note": "Read complete MSD physical page 3 and individually displayed the matching image. Definitions 2.1–2.3 fix the Grothendieck signed isobaric operator divided_difference[(1−x_(i+1))f] and longest-permutation staircase; Theorem 2.5's cited pipe-dream formula fixes degree-wise sign (−1)^(degree−length). These conventions agree with the signed-layer homogenization in Chern flow. The pipe-dream simplicial-complex theorems are cited source inputs with proofs outside this three-page selection, not new checked proof claims. Exact support versus signed-coefficient conjectures remain separated."
        },
        {
          "UTC": "2026-10-07T21:34:08.602046+00:00",
